    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). The audit output confirms the new behavior end-to-end:\n\n```\nAUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"NSWV22716E6609E7\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nHere `NSWV22716E6609E7` = region `NSWV2` + FY `27` + hash `16E6609E` + Luhn `7`.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** (a fixed `V2` tag mixed into every identifier, so no V1 value recurs):\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.memberId(...)` \u2014 region segment is now `regionFromPostcode(postcode) + \"V2\"` (e.g. `NSWV2`); the Luhn check digit recomputes over the tagged base.\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.householdId(...)` \u2014 hashes `normalizedLastName|postcode|V2`.\n- `IdentityKeys.identityKey(...)` \u2014 hashes `telephone|email|soundex(lastName)|V2` (a new public `VERSION_TAG` constant is the single source of the tag, reused by the controller).\n\n**Keeping user-facing fields plain (no `V2` tag)** \u2014 the mapper no longer parses the (now-tagged) memberId:\n- `locality` derives the plain region directly from the postcode (`NSW`, \u2026), so `timezone` and the owner-segment region stay plain.\n- `fiscalYear` derives from the registration date instead of the memberId region prefix.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` \u2192 regenerated DTOs):\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema nesting `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`; these are removed from the top level.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` (2).\n- `OwnerMapper` maps the nested `identity` object and `apiVersion`.\n\n**Audit schema v2**:\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` now emits `schemaVersion: 2` and an `ownerSegment` recomputed from the version-2 identity (plain region).\n\nRequest fields are unchanged.\n\nOne interpretation call worth flagging: the spec's audit sentence (\"\u2026and recompute the owner segment from the version-2 identity\") was ambiguous, so I both added `ownerSegment` to the v2 audit event and kept the DTO's `ownerSegment` derivation consistent with the v2 identity's plain region \u2014 covering either reading. There's only one visible test (response-shape); the identifier/audit algorithms follow the most literal reading of the spec since no test pins their exact values.",
