    "probe_text": "The POST `/api/owners` endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:893-958`). Here is everything applied, in execution order. I've tagged each step as **[V]** validation (can reject the request) or **[S]** side-effect (mutates state, the payload, or emits output).\n\n## Precondition\n- **[V] Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`; caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role (line 893).\n\n## In `addOwner`, in order\n\n1. **[S] Idempotency replay check** (896-905) \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` request header. If present and already recorded, returns the previously created owner (HTTP 200) and **skips everything below** \u2014 no new owner is created.\n\n2. **[S] Address normalization** (906, `applyAddress`) \u2014 resolves structured (`addressLine1`/`addressLine2`) vs. flat `address`, trims, collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, expands abbreviations (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE), and writes the composed `address` and normalized line fields back into the DTO.\n\n3. **[V] Required-fields check** (907, `validateRequiredFields`) \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank (address is checked *after* normalization). \u2192 `RequiredFieldsMissingException` (400) listing each missing field.\n\n4. **[S] Registration-date defaulting** (908-910) \u2014 if `registrationDate` is null, defaults to `LocalDate.now()`.\n\n5. **[V] Future-date check** (911-914) \u2014 a supplied `registrationDate` after the server date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n\n6. **[S] Business-day roll-forward** (915-916, `toBusinessDay`) \u2014 advances weekends and fixed public holidays to the next business day, and writes the adjusted date back to the DTO.\n\n7. **[V] Daily-owner-limit check** (917, `rejectDailyOwnerLimit`) \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners already carry that (effective) `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`.\n\n8. **[V] City-capacity check** (918, `rejectCityAtCapacity`) \u2014 if the city (compared case-insensitively, trimmed) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n9. **[V] Postcode validation** (919, `validatePostcode`) \u2014 if a postcode is present it must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) it must fall in that region's range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException`. Absent postcode is allowed.\n\n10. **[V] + [S] Telephone normalization** (920-921, `normalizeTelephone`) \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets, forms E.164 (assumes `+61`, drops a leading 0 when no `+`), requires 8\u201315 digits, and enforces exact national length for recognized codes (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException`. The normalized value is written back to the DTO.\n\n11. **[V] + [S] Email normalization** (922-923, `normalizeEmail`) \u2014 optional; if present must match the syntactic pattern (\u2192 `InvalidEmailException`), is lower-cased, and its domain must not be a disposable domain (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com) (\u2192 `InvalidEmailException`). Blank/absent \u2192 stored as null. Written back to the DTO.\n\n12. **[S] Read `sharesHousehold` flag** (924).\n\n13. **[S] Compute household id** (925, `householdId`) \u2014 SHA-256 prefix of normalized lastName + postcode + version tag.\n\n14. **[S] Derive identity key** (926) \u2014 SHA-256 of telephone + email + Soundex(lastName).\n\n15. **[V] Duplicate-identity check** (927, `rejectDuplicateIdentity`) \u2014 rejects if any non-soft-deleted owner has the same full identity key \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException`.\n\n16. **[S] Soft \"possible duplicate\" detection** (928-929, `findPossibleDuplicateOf`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` is true; finds an existing active owner with the same Soundex(lastName) + postcode but a different identity key (lowest id wins). This never rejects; it only tags the new owner.\n\nThen the entity is built (`ownerMapper.toOwner`, 931) and these fields are set on it \u2014 all **[S]**:\n\n17. **possibleDuplicate / possibleDuplicateOf** (932-933) \u2014 from step 16.\n18. **memberId** (934-935) \u2014 computed (`REGION+V2 | 2-digit fiscal year | 8 hex hash | Luhn check digit`), then de-duplicated against existing member ids (appends `-n`).\n19. **householdId** (936).\n20. **householdSize** (937) \u2014 existing members with same householdId + 1.\n21. **namesakeCount** (938) \u2014 count of existing owners sharing first+last name.\n22. **bulkSignupWarning** (939) \u2014 true if > 80 owners already on that registration date.\n23. **capacityWarning** (940) \u2014 true if city already holds 40\u201349 owners.\n24. **membershipLevel** (941, `cappedMembershipLevel`) \u2014 derived level, capped at one above the max level of existing household members.\n\n25. **[S] Persist** (942, `clinicService.saveOwner`) \u2014 saves the owner (assigns its id).\n\n26. **[S] Record idempotency key** (943-945) \u2014 maps the key to the new owner id, if a key was supplied.\n\n27. **[S] Audit log \u2014 plain line** (946-948) \u2014 `AUDIT` logger: id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n\n28. **[S] Audit log \u2014 structured event** (949-952) \u2014 `AUDIT` logger emits the `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON (schemaVersion 2, monotonic seq, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, ownerSegment).\n\n29. **[S] Notification log** (953) \u2014 `NOTIFY` logger emits a welcome line (owner id, memberId).\n\n30. **[S] Build response** (954-957) \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, sets the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, returns HTTP 201 Created.\n\n### Notes\n- Validations short-circuit at the first failure, so the order above is also the order in which errors surface (e.g. required-fields errors precede telephone/email errors).\n- The duplicate/identity/capacity/namesake counts all read from `clinicService.findAllOwners()`; the identity and soft-duplicate checks exclude soft-deleted owners (`activeOwners()`), while the city-capacity, daily-limit, namesake, and household-size counts do **not** filter out soft-deleted owners.\n\nI made no changes to any files."
